# UI Components and Styling Guidelines

## Overview

This project uses a combination of Material-UI (MUI) components and custom CSS styling to create a consistent and accessible user interface for the INES survey data visualization platform.

## Technology Stack

- **UI Library**: Material-UI (MUI) v6 with Emotion
- **Icons**: Material-UI Icons
- **Charts**: Nivo (bar, boxplot, heatmap)
- **Styling**: CSS modules with custom classes
- **Utilities**: classnames for conditional styling

## Component Architecture

### 1. Component Organization

- **PascalCase** naming for all React components
- Feature-based component grouping (e.g., `SmartChart/`, `QuestionSelect/`)
- Each component folder contains:
  - Main component file (`ComponentName.tsx`)
  - Associated CSS file (`ComponentName.css`)
  - Related sub-components

### 2. Component Structure Pattern

```typescript
// Standard component structure
import { ReactNode } from 'react';
import { MUIComponent } from '@mui/material';
import './ComponentName.css';

interface ComponentNameProps {
    // Props with clear types
    children?: ReactNode;
    // ... other props
}

const ComponentName = ({ children, ...props }: ComponentNameProps) => {
    // Component logic
    
    return (
        <div className="component-container">
            {/* Component JSX */}
        </div>
    );
};

export default ComponentName;
```

## Material-UI Usage Guidelines

### 1. Core MUI Components

**Layout & Structure:**
- `Box` - For layout containers with MUI styling props
- `Container` - For responsive content containers
- `Grid` - For responsive grid layouts

**Form Components:**
- `TextField` - For text inputs
- `Autocomplete` - For searchable dropdowns
- `Switch` - For toggle controls
- `ToggleButtonGroup` / `ToggleButton` - For grouped options
- `FormControlLabel` - For labeled form controls

**Feedback & Navigation:**
- `IconButton` - For icon-based actions
- `Badge` - For notification indicators
- `Popover` - For floating menus
- `Button` - For primary actions

### 2. MUI Styling Patterns

**Inline Styling with sx prop:**
```typescript
<Box sx={{ 
    width: 280, 
    p: 2, 
    display: 'flex', 
    flexDirection: 'column', 
    gap: 2 
}}>
```

**Component Styling:**
```typescript
<IconButton
    color='primary'
    onClick={handleClick}
    title="Action description"
>
    <TuneIcon />
</IconButton>
```

## Custom CSS Guidelines

### 1. CSS File Organization

- One CSS file per component folder
- Use descriptive class names with kebab-case
- Group related styles together

### 2. CSS Naming Conventions

```css
/* Component container */
.component-name {
    /* Base styles */
}

/* Sub-elements */
.component-name__element {
    /* Element styles */
}

/* Modifiers */
.component-name--modifier {
    /* Variant styles */
}
```

### 3. Color Palette

**Primary Colors:**
- Primary blue: MUI default (`color="primary"`)
- Background: `antiquewhite` for headers
- Border: `#969696` for containers

**Semantic Colors:**
- Demography questions: `rgba(250, 235, 215, 1)` (antiquewhite)
- Warning backgrounds: `#fadcd7` (light red)
- Text secondary: `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6)`

### 4. Spacing & Layout

**Margins & Padding:**
- Container margins: `30px`
- Header padding: `12px`
- Component gaps: `16px`
- Small spacing: `6px`, `8px`

**Border Radius:**
- Large containers: `16px`
- Small elements: `20px`
- Buttons: Default MUI radius

## Component Patterns

### 1. SmartChart Pattern

The main chart container with header, content, and footer:

```typescript
<div className='graph-container'>
    <GraphHeader {...headerProps} />
    <div id="graph" ref={graphRef}>
        <ScreenshotButton />
        {chartContent}
        {warningMessage}
    </div>
    <GraphFooter />
</div>
```

### 2. Filter Menu Pattern

Popover-based filter menus with toggle controls:

```typescript
<Popover
    open={isOpen}
    anchorEl={anchorEl}
    onClose={handleClose}
    anchorOrigin={{ vertical: 'bottom', horizontal: 'left' }}
    transformOrigin={{ vertical: 'top', horizontal: 'left' }}
>
    <Box sx={{ width: 280, p: 2, display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 2 }}>
        {/* Filter controls */}
    </Box>
</Popover>
```

### 3. Select Component Pattern

Custom select with autocomplete and tooltips:

```typescript
<Autocomplete
    options={options}
    renderInput={(params) => <TextField {...params} label={label} />}
    renderOption={({ key, ...optionProps }, option) => (
        <Box 
            {...optionProps}
            key={key} 
            component='li'
            title={option.tooltipText}
            className={cx(optionProps.className, option.className)}
        >
            {option.label}
        </Box>
    )}
    value={selectedOption}
    onChange={handleChange}
/>
```

## Accessibility Guidelines

### 1. ARIA Labels & Roles

- Use `aria-label` for icon buttons
- Add `role="presentation"` for decorative elements
- Include `title` attributes for tooltips

### 2. Keyboard Navigation

- Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- Use proper focus management in modals and popovers
- Maintain logical tab order

### 3. Screen Reader Support

- Provide descriptive labels for form controls
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include alt text for images

## Responsive Design

### 1. Mobile Considerations

- Hide complex interfaces on mobile (`@media (max-width: 700px)`)
- Show mobile warning messages
- Adjust logo sizes for small screens

### 2. Flexible Layouts

- Use flexbox for responsive layouts
- Implement `flex-wrap` for wrapping elements
- Set appropriate `max-width` constraints

## Performance Guidelines

### 1. Component Optimization

- Use `useMemo` for expensive computations
- Implement proper dependency arrays in hooks
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders

### 2. Asset Optimization

- Optimize images for web delivery
- Use appropriate image formats
- Implement lazy loading where beneficial

## Best Practices

### 1. Component Design

- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use TypeScript interfaces for prop definitions
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Handle loading and empty states

### 2. Styling Approach

- Prefer MUI components over custom CSS when possible
- Use CSS for layout and positioning
- Maintain consistent spacing and typography
- Follow the established color palette

### 3. Code Organization

- Group related components together
- Use descriptive file and folder names
- Keep CSS files close to their components
- Document complex styling decisions

## Common Patterns

### 1. Conditional Styling

```typescript
import cx from 'classnames';

const className = cx(
    'base-class',
    {
        'conditional-class': condition,
        'another-class': anotherCondition
    }
);
```

### 2. Responsive Design

```css
.base-class {
    /* Default styles */
}

@media (max-width: 700px) {
    .base-class {
        /* Mobile styles */
    }
}
```

### 3. Component Composition

```typescript
// Parent component
<SmartChart>
    <BarPlot data={data} />
</SmartChart>

// Child component
const SmartChart = ({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) => {
    return (
        <div className="graph-container">
            {children}
        </div>
    );
};
```

## Migration Guidelines

When adding new components:

1. **Start with MUI components and existing components from the project** when possible
2. **Follow existing naming conventions**
3. **Use established color and spacing patterns**
4. **Implement proper TypeScript interfaces**
5. **Add appropriate accessibility attributes**
6. **Test on different desktop screen sizes**
7. **Document any deviations from patterns**
